  <h1>First Call Maintenance - SMS Terms and Conditions</h1>
  <p>Last updated: August 30, 2026</p>

  <p>By texting our maintenance request number, you agree to receive
  text messages from First Call Maintenance ("FCM") related to your
  maintenance request, including confirmation, scheduling, and status
  update messages.</p>

  <h2>Program description</h2>
  <p>This texting service allows tenants to submit maintenance requests
  and receive automated and staff-sent updates about those requests, as
  an alternative to submitting requests through the online tenant
  portal.</p>

  <h2>Message frequency</h2>
  <p>Message frequency varies based on your maintenance request
  activity. You will typically receive one message confirming receipt
  of your request, and additional messages as the request is scheduled
  and completed.</p>

  <h2>Message and data rates</h2>
  <p>Message and data rates may apply, depending on your mobile carrier
  and plan.</p>

  <h2>Opt-in and opt-out</h2>
  <p>You may opt in by texting this number to submit a maintenance
  request, by agreeing to use this number at lease signing, or verbally
  as described to you by property staff. You may opt out at any time by
  replying STOP. Reply HELP for assistance or to be connected with
  First Call Maintenance directly.</p>

  <h2>No liability for message delay or delivery failure</h2>
  <p>First Call Maintenance is not liable for delayed or undelivered
  messages. For urgent or emergency maintenance issues, tenants should
  also contact First Call Maintenance directly by phone.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>See our <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for information
  on how your data is collected and used.</p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>First Call Maintenance may update these terms from time to time.
  Continued use of the texting service constitutes acceptance of any
  changes.</p>
